From 689b41801fd905c38726814bfd8c8bf935265f49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:15:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docs(process): the P? label pauses an issue until the
 maintainer sets a priority

- AGENTS.md: Pick's search excludes `label:"P?"`; a new rule says a P?
  issue is held by the maintainer - never picked, claimed, researched or
  re-prioritised by an agent, never beside a P0/P1/P2 label, and only the
  maintainer swaps it for a real priority. Agents never file with P?.
- README.md: the Issues section explains P? for contributors.
- review-prs skill step 4: a contributor's claim comment on a P? issue is
  not mirrored; one reply says the issue is paused.

The label itself is created on GitHub (lavender, "Paused: never picked
until the maintainer sets a real priority").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md |  3 +++
 AGENTS.md                          | 13 ++++++++++++-
 README.md                          |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md
index aa71b621..f4ef489c 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md
@@ -154,6 +154,9 @@ For each line `<N> <login> <time>`:
   `<time>`: skip silently. A withdrawn claim's old comment is never
   mirrored again (without this the Withdraw pass and this one would flip
   the label every run);
+- **paused issue** (labelled `P?` - AGENTS.md "`P?` is paused"): do not
+  mirror; reply once (only if no later comment mentions `@<login>`)
+  `This issue is paused by the maintainer (P?) - it isn't open for work yet; the claim isn't recorded. It will be once the maintainer sets a priority.`;
 - **closed issue**, or **already mirrored** (`claimed` set and `<login>`
   assigned, or `claimed` set and a "Claim recorded for @<login>" reply
   exists): skip silently;
diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 8119b261..0184375b 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -60,11 +60,22 @@ go to `CHANGELOG.md`.
   the same. The skill carries the `gh` mechanics (list limits, search
   syntax, heredoc bodies, closing keywords); this law stays the rule
   where the two differ.
-- **Pick.** `gh issue list --state open --search "-label:claimed -label:blocked -label:in-review -label:needs-research"`
+- **Pick.** `gh issue list --state open --search "-label:claimed -label:blocked -label:in-review -label:needs-research -label:\"P?\""`
   (then drop any whose comments hold a live contributor claim - "A claim
   comment is a claim", below) and take the highest priority first: `P0` (wrong output, gouge, crash,
   data loss) before `P1` (wrong behaviour a user hits) before `P2` (owed
   polish), then the oldest. User-reported bugs outrank owed work.
+- **`P?` is paused, not prioritised** (user, 2026-11-09: "a P? label that
+  holds an issue paused until maintainer tells it to be changed"). An issue
+  labelled `P?` is held by the maintainer: Pick never takes it, no lane
+  slot works it, no agent claims, researches, files sub-issues for or
+  re-prioritises it, and the bug/enhancement lanes skip it the same way.
+  It carries `P?` *instead of* a `P0`/`P1`/`P2` label, never beside one -
+  an agent that finds both reports it rather than choosing. Only the
+  maintainer swaps `P?` for a real priority (or closes the issue); until
+  then agents may only read it, link it, and comment facts that belong on
+  it (e.g. a duplicate or a related fix), without changing its labels.
+  An agent filing a new issue never uses `P?` - it picks `P0`/`P1`/`P2`.
 - **Two lanes, two issues each** (user, 2026-11-07: "open up the issue
   limit to 2 bugs 2 enhancements.. as we are now just working on the latest
   issues and not the old ones"). At most four issues are worked at once: two
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index f8929a39..c08f7ce4 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -215,6 +215,12 @@ gouge, crash, data loss), then `P1` (wrong behaviour a user hits), then `P2`
 (owed polish), oldest first. Each issue carries one `P*` label and one or
 more `area:*` labels. Issues opened by an agent also carry `source:agent`.
 
+**`P?` means paused.** The maintainer puts `P?` on an issue (in place of
+`P0`/`P1`/`P2`) to hold it: nobody picks it up, claims it or changes its
+priority until the maintainer swaps `P?` for a real priority or closes it.
+Comments with relevant facts (a duplicate, a related fix) are still
+welcome.
+
 **`needs-research` issues are not work items yet.** The label marks a large
 idea with open questions (a new machine type, a documentation site, a new
 kernel): research and decisions come first, and the outcome is a set of
